==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} ''[[échalote]]'', alteration of ''eschaloigne'', from Middle Latin ''escalonia'' "onion of [[w:Ascalon|Ascalon]]".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈʃælət/|/ʃəˈlɑt/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ʃəˈlɒt/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒt}}
{{rfap|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a type of onion of the species [[Allium ascalonium]].
# a type of onion of the species [[Allium oschaninii]].
# any small onion.
# (''New Orleans'') A scallion.

